say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-00.aiff' 'An image classifier can carry millions of learned weights. But deployment asks a different question. Can we keep useful intelligence, while using less storage and less time? This is CompressKit.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-01.aiff' 'A convolutional neural network processes an image through layers. Early filters respond to simple patterns, such as edges. Deeper layers combine these patterns into features. A final classifier produces scores, and the highest score gives the prediction.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-02.aiff' 'We load a trained model and preserve an untouched copy. We export the baseline to ONNX and measure accuracy, prediction latency, and file size. Training and calibration data stay separate from the test data used for evaluation.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-03.aiff' 'The toolkit checks the CPU for low precision instruction support. Eight bit arithmetic can reduce storage, but speed depends on the hardware and runtime. We use the hardware probe to guide precision, then verify performance with actual timing.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-04.aiff' 'Structured pruning removes entire feature channels. Unlike simply setting weights to zero, this changes the dimensions of the network. A dependency graph updates connected layers together, preserving compatible shapes, including around residual connections.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-05.aiff' 'Large cuts can damage accuracy. Gradual pruning alternates smaller cuts with fine tuning. Batch normalization recalibration updates activation statistics using calibration data. It requires forward passes, without gradient based weight training. Recovery can help, but does not guarantee the original accuracy.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-06.aiff' 'The original model teaches the compressed student. The student learns from correct labels and from the teacher’s output scores. These scores contain relationships between classes. Distillation can recover useful behavior lost during pruning. The teacher is not needed when the student is deployed.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-07.aiff' 'Quantization represents values using fewer bits. Moving from thirty two bit floats to eight bit integers reduces raw weight storage by about four times, for the same number of weights. Calibration determines suitable ranges. Total file reduction varies, and some operations may remain in floating point.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-08.aiff' 'When rounding damages accuracy, quantization aware training simulates reduced precision during training. The weights adapt before final quantization. In our pipeline, the final deployment quantization comes after structural changes and training.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-09.aiff' 'Automatic mode starts with quantization. If only accuracy fails, it can protect sensitive layers, then try quantization aware training and distillation. If size or latency fails, it explores pruning. Each candidate is measured. The search stops when the requirements are met, if a suitable configuration is found.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-10.aiff' 'In our recorded ResNet fifty six run, model size fell from three point two eight to zero point five three megabytes. Latency improved by two point two five times. Accuracy changed from ninety three point one eight to ninety point five zero percent: a loss of two point six eight percentage points.'
say -v Samantha -r 158 -o '/Users/bhagyeshjoshi/Developer/Model Compression ToolKit./presentation-video/voice-11.aiff' 'The final output is an ONNX model, accompanied by an HTML report and machine readable results. A new image passes through the compressed model to produce a prediction. CompressKit connects established techniques with hardware awareness, automatic decisions, and honest measurement.'
